{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions","id":1178612,"title":"Do mages police monetary transactions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-23T17:36:14-08:00","id":1178612,"title":"Do mages police monetary transactions?","content":"In cannon, would there be a group that would try to stop me to go back in time to buy 100k of bitcoins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12483-ale137","name":"ale137","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:57:38-08:00","id":1178623,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know the answer to this, but If you are powerful enough to go back that far without devastating consequences, that seems like a silly way to spend your time, no pun intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:03:43-08:00","id":1178628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178623#post1178623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know the answer to this, but If you are powerful enough to go back that far without devastating consequences, that seems like a silly way to spend your time, no pun intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, the Seers serving Mammon will just undercut its value by banning its use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T18:06:16-08:00","id":1178630,"title":"","content":"Probably not unless you did something that was damaging to history along the way in which case you'd probably get a visit from Seers or Guardians (Or other offended parties) that have Shielded themselves from temporal tampering.<br /> <br /> History in this case is very specific to the people that might be annoyed with you for whatever reason, not in the broad butterfly effect sense.<br /> <br /> So in essence, if you fucked up someone else's plans as a result of your tinkering, you might gain an enemy, but if you didn't then you probably won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T22:50:17-08:00","id":1178686,"title":"","content":"It's kinda frightening to think of all the stuff you'd witness getting retroactively changed with Time Shielding.<br /> <br /> Well, if it weren't for the fact that most Magely Time travelers (who'll actually do something to the &quot;present&quot; with their powers) are Masters, and far more than likely to smash your Clash of Wills pool into tiny little pieces with their casting/alterations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T23:16:23-08:00","id":1178689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions#post1178612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In cannon, would there be a group that would try to stop me to go back in time to buy 100k of bitcoins?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not mages, but the Lodge of the Clocktower and the Tindalosi hunt prey that meddle with the natural order of time. Also definitely seems like something angels would jump on.<br /> <br /> It really doesn't seem like something a mage group would be concerned with, beyond the attention totally-not-a-wizard would get for suddenly becoming rich and the comparatively petty use of magic. You might have a group of Banishers or Legacy that are more focused on it but they probably wouldn't be widespread. Some individual mages might think it was seedy, but that's probably nothing out of the ordinary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T03:34:14-08:00","id":1178714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178689#post1178689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">beyond the attention totally-not-a-wizard would get for suddenly becoming rich and the comparatively petty use of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The retroactivity of time edits means there\u2019s nothing sudden about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T03:55:54-08:00","id":1178716,"title":"","content":"I can imagine many factions who would be very interested in monitoring such things. I think a big majority of newly Awakened mages who haven't been introduced to the awakened society will use their magic for monetary gain, so it is a way to find new mages.<br /> <br /> Also, if someone makes big transactions it means something big is about to happen which is good to at least glance at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:45:13-08:00","id":1178740,"title":"","content":"Considering how many other ways a mage could gain money unless you change something else that another group cares about then i dont think anybody would come after you. You'd have to step on some other groups toes for them to seriously come after you.<br /> <br /> And if the goal is to make money, why not just go back and buy a winning lottery ticket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:32:10-08:00","id":1178756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178740#post1178740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how many other ways a mage could gain money unless you change something else that another group cares about then i dont think anybody would come after you. You'd have to step on some other groups toes for them to seriously come after you.<br /> <br /> And if the goal is to make money, why not just go back and buy a winning lottery ticket?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lottos are too high profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:50:56-08:00","id":1178767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178756#post1178756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lottos are too high profile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we please not talk about this again?<br /> <br /> The profile of it doesn\u2019t matter because it\u2019s just an ST decision of what level of consequences there should e for doing it, you could do it though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-24-2018, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:35:34-08:00","id":1178780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178767#post1178767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we please not talk about this again?<br /> <br /> The profile of it doesn\u2019t matter because it\u2019s just an ST decision of what level of consequences there should e for doing it, you could do it though</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there a big argument about this topic?<br /> <br /> I just meant neighbors knocking on your door, telemarketers harassing you, etc. Nothing CofD specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:51:51-08:00","id":1178785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1178780#post1178780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there a big argument about this topic?<br /> <br /> I just meant neighbors knocking on your door, telemarketers harassing you, etc. Nothing CofD specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, kicked off by almost exactly the same original question, and again any consequences of winning the lottery is entirely up to ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T11:52:25-08:00","id":1178891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions#post1178612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In cannon, would there be a group that would try to stop me to go back in time to buy 100k of bitcoins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely that no one would have to stop you, because that kind of purchase early on is going to drastically alter the way the currency developed.<br /> <br /> To answer the deeper question, that depends entirely on how the ST wants to run his game. I have been, and always will be, of the opinion that Mages have more important shit to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T18:07:07-08:00","id":1179033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions#post1178612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In cannon, would there be a group that would try to stop me to go back in time to buy 100k of bitcoins?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have that kind of Time, you probably have enough Fate to easily just guess the winning powerball lottery ticket. Of course that exposes you to public scrutiny which might mean Seers on your butt. Or might mean nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T22:49:31-08:00","id":1179117,"title":"","content":"I'll echo the others and say I don't see much happening just for this. It's possible that unless you were featured in a news story about bitcoin or walked in front of a mage with time sight while in the past no one would even notice. <br /> <br /> Definitely, there are acanthus using fate spells for profit in far more noticeable ways, such as just casting spells that make them just so happen to find money all over the place. <br /> <br /> &quot;Find a $100 bill, pick it up, and then all day you have good luck&quot; seems a lot more likely to attract attention than what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Though I'm thinking that if you got ridiculously and insanely rich doing stuff like this, a few hunter groups, particularly thinking of cheiron group, might be curious if you had some supernatural help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 01-25-2018, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T02:21:13-08:00","id":1179141,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Lottos being high profile?<br /> <br /> I can name the number of lotto winners i have heard about on zero fingers. Most lotteries you can choose not to go public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T02:38:35-08:00","id":1179142,"title":"","content":"Lottos could be high profile not in that the character becomes a public figure but because any lotto winners are easily found by any mage with the right Arcana looking specifically for whoever won that lotto.<br /> Hell, imagine how many Seers are interested in contacting lotto winners not because they're looking for other mages or sleepwalkers, but because every lotto winner is a newly created (and therefor untapped) source of material wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T08:47:18-08:00","id":1179216,"title":"","content":"Lottery winner names may not be as famed as celebrities, but their names are often publicly announced and they are targeted by a wide variety of people, from scammers and charities to folks who just want to marry into money. Apparently harassment is common. And of course in Chronicles you can expect a mystery cult or two to come try and spread the word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179142#post1179142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, imagine how many Seers are interested in contacting lotto winners not because they're looking for other mages or sleepwalkers, but because every lotto winner is a newly created (and therefor untapped) source of material wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also a mage who has proven themselves to care about the material things in life, and if a mage has that mindset, then the Seers might come recruiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T12:59:52-08:00","id":1179288,"title":"","content":"You all make it sound like every time a mage uses &quot;Shifting the Odds&quot; to gain resources that he gets a visit from some mage money police...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T13:11:05-08:00","id":1179292,"title":"","content":"Well, it\u2019s all just ST wanking on what they\u2019d do if they were running the scenario while posturing it as what will happen, which is false advertising. <br /> <br /> It basically boils down to: Maybe, could be one way, could be another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T14:17:34-08:00","id":1179309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179288#post1179288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all make it sound like every time a mage uses &quot;Shifting the Odds&quot; to gain resources that he gets a visit from some mage money police...</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we reading the same thread? Pretty much everyone said mages wouldn't care unless it affected them personally or was somehow catastrophic to the world at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-25-2018, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:44:30-08:00","id":1179341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179309#post1179309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we reading the same thread? Pretty much everyone said mages wouldn't care unless it affected them personally or was somehow catastrophic to the world at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have tended to focus on the drawbacks rather than on the feasibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:16:46-08:00","id":1179365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179341#post1179341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have tended to focus on the drawbacks rather than on the feasibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus staying on topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ale137</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions#post1178612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In cannon, would there be a group that would try to stop me to go back in time to buy 100k of bitcoins?</div> </div> </div> </div>ale137 wasn't asking for the mechanical viability of it, I'm guessing they already knew it was mechanically feasible, even easy. Given the abbreviated setting information in the core book it's reasonable to wonder if there might be such groups that might oppose it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:45:07-08:00","id":1179375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179365#post1179365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus staying on topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't change the fact that that is the cause of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> somewhat exasperated reaction.<br /> <br /> Now, it's true, in a setting run by a specific ST there might be an organization that monitors monetary fluctuations and the like for Mage interference, it might even be likely. It's equally true that in another specific setting run by a different ST there might be no one who cares.<br /> <br /> Which has been my point all along, the question the OP has can really only be answered by advising them to go ask their ST, or if they are the ST here are some options, but they're only as likely as you want them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:42:57-08:00","id":1179406,"title":"","content":"The Ministry of Mammon watches for sudden transfers of wealth. It is kind of Their Thing. Beyond that, do as you will. Generally speaking, sudden lottery winnings are a good way to watch for young Mages, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:04:47-08:00","id":1179532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1178612-do-mages-police-monetary-transactions?p=1179406#post1179406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ministry of Mammon watches for sudden transfers of wealth. It is kind of Their Thing. Beyond that, do as you will. Generally speaking, sudden lottery winnings are a good way to watch for young Mages, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, Mammon only cares when that wealth gets used to undercut the principles it holds. Many people get rich and go poor every day. It's hard to care about them and treat it like it was magical. It's only when someone intends to undercut the foundations of greed that mammon has setup that would cause the ministry to act.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T16:00:37-08:00","id":1179647,"title":"","content":"Exchange and flow of wealth <i>is</i> magical, is the thing. The very act of commerce itself is special; the way wealth accumulates in the hands of a few at the expense of the many <i>is</i> the god that the Ministry of Mammon worship. The Chancellor might not particularly care who is wealthy, so long as it's selfish, but whenever one individual's wealth expands at a rate faster than the growth of the economy as a whole, the Chancellor is there, with its thumb on the scales of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> The Ministry of Mammon pays attention to the flow of wealth because it is a holy communion as much as it serving a practical purpose; because every swipe of a credit card is a prayer and every down- or uptick of the stock market may contain a secret message from their divine lord. Even if it doesn't, people gaining a lot of money suddenly might also lead to a Mystery (which many Seers will interpret as a sign from the Chancellor anyway), since it's inevitably something a lot of folks with magic will put their mind to if given half a chance.<br /> <br /> But, as I said, it serves a practical purpose too, because wealth is power. Some goody-two-shoes becoming wealthy is something the Ministry of Mammon actively works to stop, because one charitable soul with a lot of power can work to undo all the harm they manage. The more well-off people are, the harder it is for the Ministry to attain its goals. The poor are more desperate for the wealth it holds, the rich are more fearful of losing their coveted position... A society where wealth is spread evenly for the benefit of all is one that the Ministry fears above all else for it is the least vulnerable to their manipulations.<br /> <br /> So ensuring that those who gain sudden wealth will only ever try to maintain it selfishly for their own ends? That's in the Ministry's interests.<br /> <br /> You want Mysteries? Look for sudden accumulation of wealth. You want to preemptively crush rivals? Look for sudden accumulation of wealth. You want messages from your god? Look for sudden accumulation of wealth. <br /> <br /> Why <i>wouldn't</i> they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:03:46-08:00","id":1179666,"title":"","content":"While I agree with most everything you're saying Axel, I do want to point out that the Chancellor wins as long as the guy getting rich is selfish. That goody-two-shoes may very well have grand intentions but chances are good that that kind of money is a strong temptation. If that isn't true, the Exarch's power weakens, so the ministry would need to get involved. If a supposedly moral figure falls to that temptation, though, that's a particularly <b>big</b> win.<br /> <br /> So, while I think they will certainly track money exchanging hands and accumulating anywhere, I think they'd welcome outsiders opening themselves up to their Exarch's influence like that. Even enemies are pretty interchangeable, that way.<br /> <br /> (Speaking of which: Mammon members should have access to spells that can track something sympathetically through currency transactions and be able to identify and target &quot;wealth&quot; as a specific singular item, IMO. The latter would mean that they could find some part of a fortune and figure out how much there was by simply scrying it or something. Going from &quot;this is a pool of accumulated wealth&quot; to &quot;this is the owner of said pool&quot; should be a bit more difficult but quite possible.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:46:36-08:00","id":1179924,"title":"","content":"Mages might not take much interest in sudden accumulations of wealth but the IRS does and the last thing a Mage wants is to be the subject of an insider trading or fraud investigation, so be subtle.<br /> \u200bAs far as Mages though, the only one I could see taking an interest in your Bitcoin deal is the Arch-Mage who created the thing in an attempt to create a new symbol for currency that will fuel his Ascension. Screw that up for him and you will definitely be receiving a visit you won't soon forget (or you will, along with everything else).<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you want an example of how the Seers respond to such things then I think Dave's treatment of the Las Vegas casinos in &quot;The Man Comes Around&quot; would serve you well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}